    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Founding-Program-Director--Engineering_R-096845": {
      "title": "Founding Program Director, Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Founding Program Director, Engineering Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Natural & Applied Science Proposed Minimum Salary $8,333.34 monthly Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University–Victoria seeks a full-time, 12-month faculty member for an appointment as a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor or a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice to serve as the Founding Director of the new Bachelor of Science programs in Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, and Software Engineering. The Founding Director will provide leadership for launching, promoting, and advancing these programs and will teach courses within the programs. Qualifications: The Bachelor of Science (BS) degrees in engineering are designed to serve the community in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. The Founding Director will serve as a primary point of contact for Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), with a primary focus on developing and supporting the BS in Civil Engineering, Software Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering with a focus on the intersections between these disciplines. They will also need to satisfy the expectations of Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) and ABET in terms of academic credentials, as well as all other employment qualifications of the University. The programs are anticipated to be open for enrollment Fall 2027. The Founding Director will be employed by A&M-Victoria and will teach face-to-face courses within the University’s academic programs. Victoria is about two hours driving time from Houston, Corpus Christi, Austin, and San Antonio. The Founding Program Director reports to Dean of the College of Natural and Applied Science, working within the Department of Engineering and Aviation Sciences, and has both administrative and instructional responsibilities. The successful candidate should demonstrate the following qualifications: · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage professional, community, industry, and student audiences. · Ability to plan and implement activities that increase the visibility and profile of the A&M-Victoria Agribusiness concentration within the regional community and agricultural industry. · Demonstrated commitment to supporting and working effectively with students from diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds, as well as students with disabilities. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will be expected to: · Teach classes in service of A&M-Victoria engineering programs, in line with academic credentials and professional experience. Teaching assignments will include face-to-face classes in Victoria, Texas. · Promote A&M-Victoria engineering programs in the greater Victoria region in collaboration with the Division of Enrollment Management. · Direct and oversee the development and equipping of necessary lab and classroom teaching spaces for the proposed engineering degrees. · Be responsible for administrative matters of the department, including teaching, laboratory and research facilities; class rotations and scheduling; budget; and equipment. · Maintain good working relationships with the Independent School Districts and community colleges in Victoria and the surrounding area, as well as with industry partners in the region. · Advise students interested in admission to A&M-Victoria for study in engineering. · Coordinate with the Center for Student Success to ensure that engineering students receive academic advising necessary to foster academic success. · Participate in student activities and campus life and facilitate mentoring for engineering students with industry professionals. · Engage in philanthropic development and community engagement in collaboration with the Office of University Advancement. · Actively participate in affairs of the University, including assisting the engineering programs achieve and maintain ABET program accreditation. · Coordinate with the Career Development Center to develop industry partnerships beneficial to A&M-Victoria and the engineering programs. · Perform other duties as may be necessary and assigned. Because of the University’s outreach mission to serve the broader Texas Gulf Coast region, the position may require travel and occasional work outside of normal business hours. For more information about Texas A&M University-Victoria’s programs and mission, visit www.tamuv.edu. Education and Experience : The position requires an earned master’s degree in engineering or engineering technology. Because this is a professional-track appointment, relevant industry experience in engineering as well as industrial design is expected. An earned doctorate in engineering with prior classroom experience and a knowledge of ABET accreditation and experience leading a program through accreditation is preferred. A current licensure as a professional engineer (mechanical or civil) is strongly preferred. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values : Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the SACSCOC, and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here. Application: Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit here. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact Dolores Guerrero (GuerreroD5@tamuv.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Founding-Program-Director--Aviation_R-096759-2": {
      "title": "Founding Program Director, Aviation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Founding Program Director, Aviation Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Natural & Applied Science Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University–Victoria seeks a full-time, 12-month faculty member for an appointment as a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor or a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice to serve as the Founding Director of the new Bachelor of Science in Aviation program to promote and enhance the degree and teach within the program. Qualifications: Aviation is a new Bachelor of Science (BS) degree designed to serve the community in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. The Founding Director will serve as a primary point of contact for Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), with a primary focus on developing and supporting the BS in Aviation. The Aviation Science Program offers Professional Pilot and Aviation Management pathways. Flight training through a contracted provider will be conducted at the Victoria Regional Airport. The Founding Director will be employed by A&M-Victoria and will teach face-to-face courses within the University’s academic programs. Victoria is about two hours driving time from Houston, Corpus Christi, Austin, and San Antonio. The Victoria region offers great flying weather throughout the year, Class D airspace, a tower-controlled airport, and vast airspace for flight training. The Founding Program Director reports to Dean of the College of Natural and Applied Science, working within the Department of Engineering and Aviation Sciences, and has both administrative and instructional responsibilities, which may include classroom, flight, or ground school instruction. The proportions of each will be negotiated upon hire. The successful candidate should demonstrate the following qualifications: · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage professional, community, industry, and student audiences. · Ability to plan and implement activities that increase the visibility and profile of the A&M-Victoria Agribusiness concentration within the regional community and agricultural industry. · Demonstrated commitment to supporting and working effectively with students from diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds, as well as students with disabilities. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will be expected to: · Plan and direct all aspects of the aviation program including curriculum development, Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) regulatory compliance, flight operations, scheduling, and accreditation. · Carry out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the College’s policies and applicable laws. · Oversee all operations of the aviation degree program including the flight training contractor. · Oversee all operations of the aviation degree program including the flight training contractor. · Teach courses within the aviation program, including ground school and other subjects as appropriate. Teaching assignments will include face-to-face classes in Victoria, Texas. · Plan and conduct activities that raise the profile of the A&M-Victoria Aviation Science Program within the community and industry. · Actively participate in student recruitment and coordinating with the Division of Enrollment Management to develop recruiting material. · Facilitate mentoring for aviation students with industry professionals and fostering graduate placement. · Identify resource requirements and managing Aviation Program budgets. · Oversee compliance with Aviation Accreditation Board International (AABI) requirements. · Supervise and administer Aviation Program extra-curricular activities and engage with professional organizations, including the National Intercollegiate Flying Association (NIFA). · Perform other duties as may be assigned. Because of the University’s outreach mission to serve the broader Texas Gulf Coast region, the position may require travel and occasional work outside of normal business hours. For more information about Texas A&M University-Victoria’s programs and mission, visit www.tamuv.edu . Education and Experience: The position requires an earned master’s degree in aviation or an equivalent degree or relevant field. Because this is a professional-track appointment, relevant industry experience in aviation and/or flight operations and aviation management is expected (e.g., service as a commercial or military pilot). The position also requires Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) instrument and single-engine land or multi-engine land commercial pilot ratings. Experience as a flight and/or ground school instructor, previous classroom teaching experience in a higher education setting, Single-engine land and multi-engine land pilot ratings, and CFI/Instrument rating is preferred. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact Dolores Guerrero ( GuerreroD5@tamuv.edu ) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Tenure-Track-Faculty---Special-Education--ABA-_R-096742-2": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty - Special Education (ABA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Tenure-Track Faculty - Special Education (ABA) Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Education & Health Professions Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Job Description Texas A&M University-Victoria College of Education and Health Professions is seeking a qualified tenure-track professor to teach graduate special education Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) classes.  A&M–Victoria is a Hispanic-serving institution, located in the Coastal Bend region of southeast Texas. The campus is in Victoria, TX, approximately 2 hours from Houston, Austin, Corpus Christi, and San Antonio. A&M–Victoria enrolls approximately 3,300 students.  This position is based in Victoria, TX. The successful applicant is expected to play a role in supporting graduate teaching, thus contributing to campus and student life in Victoria. Our Special Education department offers an M.Ed in Special Education Applied Behavior Analysis to prepare students to become credentialed behavior analysts.   The position requires the Clinical Professor to teach courses each fall and spring semester, advise students and oversee the program including taking steps toward accreditation.  Position summary:  The position is based in Victoria, Texas.   It is a nine-month clinical track position. The sum of responsibilities include teaching graduate classes; overseeing the SPED ABA program including program and curriculum development toward accreditation; collecting data for program review and advising students. Candidates are expected to maintain excellence in teaching; participate in course and program development; perform other duties as assigned by the Dean of the College of Education and Health Professions and the Chair of the Department of Educational Leadership, Postsecondary Education, and Special Education, and perform all other related activities as required. This position will start in Fall 2026 and is renewable on an annual basis. Opportunities for summer teaching might be available based on demand and departmental need. Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Applied Behavior Analysis, Special Education or Educational Psychology    Experience in special education in K-12 public schools working with students with disabilities Experience teaching online BCBA-D credential Ability to guide students in experimental research for capstone projects For questions about the position, please contact Mary Lasater ( LasaterM@tamuv.edu ) Applicants must apply online and include: * A cover letter * A current curriculum vitae *A list of three professional references who are in a position to know the applicant’s expertise, with at least two addressing teaching effectiveness; letters of recommendation will be requested during the final stages of the search. * Evidence of effective teaching, such a statement of teaching philosophy or student evaluations, if available *Copies of all college transcripts (official transcripts will be required of all finalists)  Salary is competitive. Review of applications will begin on September 17, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values : Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
