    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Founding-Program-Director--Bachelor-of-Business-Administration---Agribusiness_R-096816": {
      "title": "Founding Program Director, Bachelor of Business Administration - Agribusiness",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Founding Program Director, Bachelor of Business Administration - Agribusiness Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Business Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University–Victoria seeks a full-time, 12-month faculty member for an appointment as a tenure-track Associate or Full Professor or a non-tenure-track Professor of Practice to serve as the Founding Director of the BBA, Agribusiness program to promote and enhance the Agribusiness concentration and teach within the program. Qualifications: Agribusiness is a new concentration within the Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA) degree designed to serve the agricultural community in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. The Founding Director will serve as a primary point of contact for Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), with a primary focus on developing and supporting the BBA concentration in Agribusiness. The Founding Director will be employed by A&M-Victoria and will teach face-to-face courses within the University’s academic programs. Accordingly, the successful candidate must meet the academic credentialing requirements of Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) and AACSB, as well as all other employment qualifications established by the University. The successful candidate should demonstrate the following qualifications: · Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage professional, community, industry, and student audiences. · Ability to plan and implement activities that increase the visibility and profile of the A&M-Victoria Agribusiness concentration within the regional community and agricultural industry. · Demonstrated commitment to supporting and working effectively with students from diverse academic, socioeconomic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds, as well as students with disabilities. Responsibilities: The individual in this position will be expected to: · Teach multiple courses each semester, primarily at the undergraduate level, through face-to-face instruction in Victoria, Texas. · Provide leadership for the recruitment, growth, and ongoing development of the Agribusiness concentration, including course and curriculum development. · Respond effectively and sensitively to the educational needs of a diverse population of current and prospective students. · Engage in university and professional service and collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, industry partners, community organizations, and other stakeholders. · Perform other duties as assigned by the dean and department chair. Because of the University’s outreach mission to serve the broader Texas Gulf Coast region, the position may require travel and occasional work outside of normal business hours. For more information about Texas A&M University-Victoria’s programs and mission, visit www.tamuv.edu. Education and Experience: The position requires an earned master’s degree in business or agribusiness. Because this is a professional-track appointment, relevant industry experience in agribusiness is expected. An earned doctorate in business or agribusiness and prior teaching experience in higher education are preferred. Texas A&M University-Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the SACSCOC, and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact information for three references. If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Yixi Ning (NingY@TAMUV.edu). All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Exec-Admin-Asst-to-VP-Enrl-Mgm_R-096644": {
      "title": "Exec Admin Asst to VP Enrl Mgm",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Exec Admin Asst to VP Enrl Mgm Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Enrollment Management Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Executive Administrative Assistant to the Vice President for Enrollment Management, under general supervision, provides high-level administrative, operational, and executive support to the Vice President and the Enrollment Management division. Work involves coordinating the administrative operations of the division, supporting executive priorities and initiatives, and serving as a key resource and liaison for departments within Enrollment Management. Exercises discretion, independent judgment, initiative, and sound judgment with respect to matters of significance and serves as a strategic administrative partner to the division. Responsibilities: Coordinates complex calendars, meetings, appointments, travel, and other activities for the Vice President and Enrollment Management. Proactively identifies and resolves scheduling conflicts and coordinates competing priorities to maximize efficiency. Provides administrative guidance and support to the Vice President, directors, managers, and staff within Enrollment Management. Coordinates and monitors action items, assignments, deadlines, and deliverables and provides follow-up and status updates. Drafts and manages executive correspondence, communications, reports, presentations, agendas, briefing materials, talking points, and other documents. Coordinates communication and follow-up with internal and external stakeholders on behalf of the Vice President and division. Assists with compiling reports, researching and evaluating information, maintaining records and documentation, and preparing materials to support executive decision-making, divisional planning, and operational activities. Supports HR-related administrative functions for Enrollment Management, including recruitment and hiring processes, employee documentation, onboarding, personnel actions, Workday tasks, and coordination with Human Resources. Assists with divisional budget and fiscal activities, including purchasing, invoices, expense tracking, budget documentation, financial records, and related administrative processes. Coordinates with appropriate university offices to facilitate timely and accurate financial transactions. Communicates and assists with interpreting university and divisional policies, procedures, standards, and administrative requirements. Responds to inquiries, resolves routine administrative matters, and appropriately escalates sensitive or complex issues. Anticipates executive and divisional needs, identifies potential scheduling, administrative, or operational concerns, and recommends solutions or process improvements before they affect divisional operations. Plans and coordinates logistical and administrative support for meetings, events, conferences, special functions, and Enrollment Management initiatives. Provides on-site support and coordinates necessary resources, materials, and arrangements. Coordinates travel arrangements, registrations, itineraries, and related documentation for the Vice President and designated staff. May prepare, review, and process travel reimbursements in accordance with university policies. Maintains organized, accurate, and confidential records, files, correspondence, and documentation to support institutional continuity, accountability, compliance, and effective divisional operations. Develops and maintains a working knowledge of Enrollment Management departments, programs, processes, systems, organizational structures, and priorities to effectively anticipate needs and support executive decision-making and operational execution. Serves as a central administrative liaison and resource for Enrollment Management departments, coordinating departmental requests, special projects, university initiatives, and cross-functional activities to promote communication and collaboration throughout the division. Monitors divisional priorities, action items, deadlines, and outstanding deliverables and provides leadership with timely updates regarding progress, follow-up needs, and potential concerns. Exercises sound judgment, discretion, professionalism, and confidentiality when handling sensitive executive, personnel, financial, student, and institutional information. Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Three years of related experience. Experience supporting executive leadership or senior-level administrators preferred. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of administrative practices, procedures, and organizational operations. Knowledge of HR administrative processes, budgeting, purchasing, financial documentation, and general office operations preferred. Knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet, presentation, calendar, and other office productivity applications. Ability to manage multiple priorities, competing deadlines, and complex administrative responsibilities. Ability to exercise independent judgment, discretion, initiative, and sound decision-making. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Strong planning, organizational, problem-solving, and project coordination skills. Ability to anticipate needs, resolve issues, and work proactively with limited direction. Ability to research, compile, evaluate, and communicate information effectively. Ability to maintain confidentiality and establish effective working relationships with executives, administrators, faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders. Ability to adapt to changing priorities and work effectively in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. Starting salary for this position is $3,657.33 monthly and is negotiable depending on education and experience. A Closer Look at A&M-Victoria Texas A&M University-Victoria is a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world and is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. A&M-Victoria promotes economic development and advances the quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, we are driven by a relentless pursuit of excellence. As a next-generation university, we redefine the boundaries of higher education, creating opportunities for students from all backgrounds to excel. Our unwavering focus on student success and research innovation sets us apart, positioning A&M-Victoria as a model for universities of the future. Our History Since our establishment in 1973, we have grown into a vibrant institution with a reputation for academic excellence and a dedication to student success. At Texas A&M University-Victoria, our history is a testament to our commitment to providing quality education and fostering academic achievement. Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System – making it the 12th campus in the System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. City Location A regional hub 30 miles inland from the Gulf of Mexico, Victoria is a town of 65,000 located about two hours from Houston, Austin, San Antonio and Corpus Christi. Located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas, A&M-Victoria serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Mission Statement  Texas A&M University-Victoria (A&M-Victoria), a dynamic destination institution serving Texas and the world, is dedicated to providing every student with educational and leadership opportunities to become a successful professional and an engaged global citizen. Innovative educational activities challenge students to make meaningful connections between their learning and their lives in a complex world. Texas A&M University-Victoria promotes economic development and advances quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. Our Goals Continually enhance the quality of our student experience. Promote and expand access to education. Increase community engagements and increase public events for diverse audiences on our campuses. Promote a culture of institutional identification among stakeholders Academic Excellence Several of A&M-Victoria’s academic degree programs have drawn top rankings from organizations including College Consensus, Intelligent.com and Research.com. Our Accreditations include: SACSCOC Accredited, AACSB Accredited, ABET Accredited, CACREP Accredited, NASP Accredited, and TASP Accredited The Texas A&M University System is one of the largest and most impactful higher education systems in the country, with an annual budget of $7.3 billion. Its statewide network includes 12 universities, a comprehensive health science center, eight state agencies, Texas A&M–Fort Worth and the Texas A&M–RELLIS. The System serves nearly 180,000 students and reaches millions more through service, research and outreach programs each year. With nearly $1.6 billion in annual research expenditures, the System fuels innovation, supports communities and drives Texas’ economy forward. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
