    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Instructor-or-Assistant-Professor-of-English--Fiction--Creative-Writing-_R-097533": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of English (Fiction, Creative Writing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructor or Assistant Professor of English (Fiction, Creative Writing) Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A & M-Victoria seeks one full-time, non-tenure Instructor (with MFA) or one full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor (with doctoral degree) of English (Fiction, Creative Writing) with a start date of August 2027. Qualifications : The Department of Humanities at Texas A & M-Victoria invites applications for a tenure-track position in English. Qualified applicants must have a doctoral degree (Assistant Professor) or MFA (Instructor) by August 15, 2027 in English, creative writing, or a related field; demonstrate excellence in teaching; provide evidence of scholarly, creative, and professional activities; and be willing to teach service courses offered by the English faculty as needed, including composition and professional writing. Other classes would be assigned in accordance with department needs and the new hire’s teaching interests. As preferred qualifications, we seek a candidate specializing in fiction. Additional experience in creative nonfiction, genre fiction, publishing, and/or professional editing is welcome. Experience mentoring undergraduate writers and supporting first-generation students is especially welcomed. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in a small but vigorous English program, including fiction workshops, composition, and other courses aligned with program needs and the candidate’s expertise. Depending on program needs and qualifications, the candidate may also have opportunities to teach literature courses and/or contribute to the MFA program. The candidate will hold regular office hours on campus; provide student-centered instruction and support for undergraduate writers; participate in course and program development; maintain an active agenda of scholarly, creative, and/or professional activity; perform appropriate college and professional service; and work cooperatively with students, faculty, and staff. The candidate will also be required to maintain a consistent campus presence. This is a nine-month appointment. The annual teaching load is 24 credit hours (4/4) for an Assistant Professor appointment or 30 credit hours (5/5) for an Instructor appointment, depending on the candidate’s qualifications. The successful candidate will begin employment in Fall 2027. Values : Texas A & M-Victoria Values: Together We Rise · W isdom · E xcellence · R espect · I ntegrity · S tudents · E mpathy Setting : Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics, and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . Application: Review of applications will begin October 24, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application addressing qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position and to apply, visit here . If you have any questions related to the search, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Professor Raymond Stricklin (StricklinR@TAMUV.edu) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUV_External/job/Victoria-TAMUV/Executive-Director-Of-Enrollment-Management_R-097782": {
      "title": "Executive Director Of Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-05\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Title Executive Director Of Enrollment Management Agency Texas A&M University - Victoria Department Enrollment Management Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Victoria, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Provides strategic and operational leadership for enrollment management functions, including student recruitment, admissions processing, and related enrollment technology. Leads the development and execution of enrollment strategies and processes designed to support institutional enrollment goals, improve the prospective and incoming student experience, enhance operational efficiency, and support data-informed decision-making. Provides leadership and oversight to directors, managers, and staff responsible for assigned Enrollment Management functions. Position Description Evaluates enrollment processes and the prospective student journey to identify service gaps, operational inefficiencies, and opportunities to improve recruitment, admissions, and enrollment outcomes.  Uses enrollment, recruitment, admissions, and operational data to evaluate performance, identify trends and opportunities, establish priorities, and support strategic and operational decision-making.  Provides leadership for enrollment-related technology and systems associated with recruitment, admissions processing, communications, applicant management, and related business processes.  Develops, recommends, implements, and evaluates policies, procedures, workflows, and business practices related to assigned Enrollment Management functions.  Interprets and applies applicable University and Texas A&M University System policies and procedures and relevant state and federal requirements within assigned areas of responsibility.  Collaborates with University leadership, academic and administrative departments, System offices, and other internal and external stakeholders to coordinate enrollment initiatives, resolve issues, and advance institutional enrollment priorities.  Provides fiscal and resource oversight for assigned recruitment, marketing, travel, operational, and staffing resources. Monitors expenditures and promotes responsible use of university resources.  Represents Enrollment Management and the University in meetings, committees, professional activities, community engagement, and interactions with external organizations as assigned.  Develops and monitors operational goals, performance measures, and service expectations for assigned areas and implements improvements to support accountability and continuous improvement.  Supports the Vice President of Enrollment Management in the development and implementation of divisional priorities, enrollment initiatives, and special projects.  Performs other duties and projects as assigned.  Supervisor/Subordinates Supervisor:   Vice President of Enrollment Management Subordinates:   Provides direct supervision to director, assistant director, and other assigned positions within Enrollment Management. Provides indirect leadership to employees reporting through subordinate supervisors and managers. Job Requirements Education and Experience Bachelor's degree in an applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience.  Ten years of related experience, including progressively responsible experience in enrollment management, recruitment, admissions, or related higher education functions.  Experience providing leadership or supervision within enrollment management or a related functional area.  Preferred: Master's degree in an applicable field.  Progressive leadership experience overseeing multiple enrollment-related functions.  Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of enrollment management, student recruitment, admissions, and related higher education practices.  Knowledge of principles and practices related to strategic enrollment planning and enrollment operations.  Knowledge of applicable institutional policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements.  Ability to lead and manage multiple functional areas and provide effective supervision and leadership to directors, managers, and staff.  Ability to develop, implement, and evaluate strategies, processes, procedures, and operational improvements.  Ability to analyze enrollment and operational data and use information to support decision-making.  Ability to identify complex operational issues, evaluate alternatives, and develop effective solutions.  Strong organizational, planning, and project management skills.  Strong written, verbal, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills.  Ability to establish priorities and manage multiple initiatives and deadlines.  Ability to exercise discretion and independent judgment regarding significant operational and personnel matters.  Ability to collaborate effectively with university leadership, faculty, staff, students, System representatives, and external stakeholders.  Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive student, personnel, and institutional information.  Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a complex higher education environment.  PC Skills Knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet, presentation, database, student information, customer relationship management, reporting, and other enrollment-related technology and systems. Working Conditions Standard office environment. Position may require travel and driving a University or personal vehicle for University business. May require evening, weekend, or other work outside normal business hours to support recruitment events, enrollment activities, meetings, and institutional needs. Required Documents: Resume, Cover Letter, References The salary range for this position is $105,000-$115,000 annually or commensurate with experience . Texas A&M University-Victoria Values: Together We Rise W isdom E xcellence R espect I ntegrity S tudents E mpathy Setting: Texas A&M University-Victoria is the most recent addition to the Texas A&M University System. The University was founded in 1973 as part of the University of Houston System and was transferred to the Texas A&M University System during the 89th Texas Legislative Session. A&M-Victoria is the only four-year university in a 100-mile radius and is just 30 miles from the Texas Gulf Coast. The University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution located in the Coastal Bend region of Texas. It serves the educational needs, promotes economic well-being, and advances the community and region's quality of life through teaching, research, and service excellence. The university is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC), and it offers more than 50 academic programs, as well as concentrations and certificates. The university also has several accreditations for specific areas and programs, including from the AACSB, ABET, CACREP and CCNE. In addition to its recent transition into The Texas A&M University System, A&M-Victoria is in the process of adding academic programs in three major areas: aviation, agribusiness, and engineering. In addition to academic excellence, A&M-Victoria has a thriving Athletics program that offers six competitive teams: baseball, softball, men’s and women’s soccer, and men’s and women’s golf. The Jaguars are part of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA), and the baseball, softball and soccer teams compete in the Red River Athletic Conference. The golf teams compete in the Association of Independent Institutions Conference. Learn more about Texas A&M University-Victoria's history, academic programs, and campus facilities here . All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    }
